+
+## Every sender through the pacer (W5-Dc-r1b)
+
+Built for W5-Dc-r1b against CH-15 (QH-7 to QH-10). Covers `ownerPacer` and `recallNotify` (`main.go`), `loop2Notify.send` (`loop2.go`), `followSetting.alert` (`follow.go`) and the digest's quiet wait (`digest.go`).
+
+| # | Assumption | Spec basis | If it changes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| PW1 | **The pacer is bound late.** The grants `Config` is built before the daemon makes the owner channel, so its hooks read `ownerPacer`, whose channel is set right after `daemon.Run`. Until then the hooks say not quiet, nothing urgent and no allowance: a paced approval request waits (one for an owner in active chat or a re-issued intent still goes), and the digest is not quiet but runs only after the channel is set. | CH-15 | Set the channel before the daemon serves, if the daemon gains a hook for it. |
+| PW2 | **Each caller's class (QH-9, final table).** Loops urgent security texts (`loops/secure.go`, `urgent` true) and the fork-switch alert: `security`. Loops reports and probes, forget done texts (`loop2Notify.try`), sleep's holding line, the digest outage line and grants' `Inform` notices: `update`, through `Inform`. Agent replies (`evidence`) and agent questions: `agent`, through `Notify`, unchanged. Recall take-back notices: `approval`, through `NotifyAs`, so they keep the agent prefix. The meter only journals its limit and the clock guard has no `Notify` yet (`questions.go`), so neither is a caller. | CH-15, SG-r1-2 | A grants notice that asks the owner to act before expiry (the Wi-Fi page confirmation, `gate.go` 1651) is sent as `update`: the grants `Owner` interface has only `Inform`; giving it a class is BOARD release work. |
+| PW3 | **Lock order.** The digest asks `Quiet` under its own lock and grants asks `Allowance` without its lock; both then take the owner channel's lock. The owner channel never calls the digest or the gate while holding that lock, so no cycle forms. | CH-15 | If the owner channel ever calls back into the digest under its lock, ask `Quiet` before taking the digest's lock. |
+| PW4 | **STATUS says what the pacer holds (QH-10).** `owner.Channel.HeldNote` is added for it, since the owner exposes no held count: "N texts held until HH:MM (quiet hours)." with the quiet hours' end, or "N texts held: R an hour." with the owner's rate, then "D earlier texts were dropped." when the cap dropped any. It carries no held text. The minute tick calls `Release`, which sends only outside quiet hours and within the allowance. | CH-15, OP-9 | BOARD W5-Dc-r16 asks a marker on released texts too; this line covers its STATUS half. |
